whisper.cpp
    Copyright (c) 2023-2026 The ggml authors
    MIT License. https://github.com/ggml-org/whisper.cpp
    Pinned at 2ca53bb45e38748d07b310eeb36245a7157ac882. Full license text:
    vendor/whisper.cpp/LICENSE.

These trees are pruned to what the build needs and are otherwise unmodified
upstream source. The pruning removes tests, examples, tooling and bindings for
other languages; it never edits the code that ships. Where a change was
unavoidable it is recorded in docs/vendoring.md rather than applied silently,
so a reader can always diff what is here against the pinned upstream commit.

None of this is visible in the library's exported surface: libdespia_ai.so
exports the eleven despia_ai_* ABI symbols and nothing else, so an app that
links its own ggml, llama or whisper does not collide with the copies here.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
G2P pack data
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The grapheme-to-phoneme packs are built, not vendored: no pack is in this tree,
and tools/g2p/ fetches these sources at build time under the digests below. They
are listed here anyway because a pack REDISTRIBUTES them. The lexicon becomes the
pack's LEXK and LEXV sections close to verbatim, and the letter-to-sound trees are
trained on that same lexicon, so an app that embeds a pack is shipping this work
in both derived forms. ai_package_gate.rb checks each digest and license id below
against tools/g2p/fetch_sources.py, so a source cannot be added to the builder
without being named here.

misaki (US English lexicons: us_gold.json, us_silver.json)
    Apache-2.0. https://pypi.org/project/misaki/
    misaki-0.9.4-py3-none-any.whl, sha256
    90e2eeb169786c014c429e5058d2ea6bcd02d651f2a24450ba6c9ffc0f8da15a.
    The distribution carries exactly one license file, Apache-2.0, with no NOTICE
    and no separate data license, and its English acknowledgements credit no
    external dictionary. Dictionaries are often licensed apart from the code that
    reads them; here they are not, and that was checked rather than assumed.

CMU Pronouncing Dictionary
    BSD-2-Clause. https://github.com/cmusphinx/cmudict
    cmudict.dict at commit 74790861f652b15e4ac49015a90074ad62a27690, sha256
    81917843c7f44ce2b094ac63873c2c7a4cf802040792c455ba3ca406891c3d22, with its
    LICENSE at sha256
    bd4ce8e44170a5f9f481310ca85c51de3c4f851a65e679b40e603b143bd3542a.
    An optional second lexicon tier. Pinned to a commit rather than to a branch,
    because a branch name names different bytes on different days.

espeak-ng is NOT here and is not a fallback anywhere in this package. It is
GPL-3.0, and it is the reason the upstream frontend for this alphabet could not
be used as it stands: its letter-to-sound fallback IS espeak. The replacement is
trained on the permissive lexicons above, so the trees emit the pack's own
alphabet and there is no phone-set mapping and no copyleft anywhere in the path.

Model weights are NOT part of this package and are not covered by this license.
Every model carries its own terms, recorded per catalog entry (engine is not
weights: one model's licence is not another's).
